# Docker does not read .gitignore. Without this file `COPY . .` takes the whole
# 1.1 GB of backend/, including `data/` — the SQLite database and ~900 MB of
# downloaded audio.
#
# That is not just image bloat. The prod stage mounts a named volume at
# /app/data, and Docker seeds an empty named volume from whatever the image has
# at that path — so a first boot on the server would populate it with this
# machine's library and database. Every unowned song would then be browsable and
# streamable by anyone who reached the host, which is exactly what the project's
# ground rules and its per-key isolation exist to prevent.

# The library and the database. Never in an image.
data/

# A local virtualenv (181 MB), built for this machine's Python. The image
# installs its own dependencies.
.venv/

# Secrets. Configuration reaches the container as environment variables.
.env

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Local setuptools output. Harmless but stale, and it lands in /app where the
# application runs.
build/
*.egg-info/

# Credentials mounted at runtime, never baked in (#177).
secrets/
